Introduce `x`. Establish `eq : (fun t : ℝ => om (1, γ (Multiplicative.ofAdd t)) (∑ i, pure (f i) (φ i)) x) = fun t : ℝ => ∑ i ∈ Finset.univ, om (1, γ (Multiplicative.ofAdd t)) (pure (f i) (φ i)) x`. Use function extensionality and compare the values at `t`. Simplify using `[map_sum, Finset.sum_apply]`. Rewrite using `[eq]`.

Conclude with `HasDerivAt.fun_sum (fun i _ => hder i x)`. Establish `e1 : Φ₁ = ∑ i, pure (D (f i)) (φ i)`. Use function extensionality and compare the values at `x`. Rewrite using `[Finset.sum_apply]`. Conclude with `(hd x).unique (hsum x)`.

Use `⟨T, hT, m, fun i => D (f i), φ, fun i => ⟨hDm _ (hf i).1, (hf i).2⟩, e1, ?_⟩` and prove the remaining obligations. Set `π : G.M.Pol Bs.ψ Bs.emb →ₗ[ℂ] R.Pi` to `R.p ∘ₗ (G.M.Pol Bs.ψ Bs.emb).subtype`. Establish `hπ : Function.Surjective π` using `fun y => by`. Establish `: y ∈ (G.M.Pol Bs.ψ Bs.emb).map R.p` using `hM.real.quot.onto ▸ Submodule.mem_top`. Take `⟨g, hg, e⟩` from `Submodule.mem_map.1 this`.

Conclude with `⟨⟨g, hg⟩, e⟩`. Establish `ker0 : ∀ g ∈ G.M.Pol Bs.ψ Bs.emb, R.p g = 0 → R.p (D g) = 0` using `fun g hg h0 => by`. Use `hM.real.lie γ hγ g hg 0 (zero_mem _) (D g) 0 ((hDi g hg _).2 rfl) (GlobalTheory.ThK.RealUniq.actsD_zero _) (by rw [h0, map_zero])` as an intermediate fact. Rewrite `this` using `[map_zero]`. Then use the resulting hypothesis. Set `A` to `GlobalTheory.ThK.RealUniq.induced π hπ (D.restrict hDm) (fun u hu => ker0 u.1 u.2 hu)`.

